# Agnes 2.5 Flash — findings by GLM 5.3 Flash

- Source: Agnes AI (`agnes-2.5-flash` — Agnes AI API, apihub.agnes-ai.com)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> SELF-EXCLUDED — zero verified public benchmark numbers found for this exact model/ID after a full pass over Agnes AI's official documentation (model page, wiki index, pricing), the models.dev catalog, BenchLM (not tracked — 404) and web search (no relevant third-party coverage). The vendor publishes no evaluation table and no independent harness has measured it. Saved as `.md.excluded` per the template's mandatory self-exclusion rule; verified model facts recorded below for future re-research.

## Model card

- **Name:** Agnes 2.5 Flash
- **Short description:** Agnes AI's generally available workhorse language model (2026-07, upgrade of the deprecated Agnes 2.0 Flash) for coding, agent workflows, multi-turn chat and image understanding — 512K context, tool calling, thinking mode, and OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible endpoints at list prices of $0.05/$0.15 per 1M with a $0 trial tier. Part of the Agnes family (2.0 Flash → 2.5 Flash → 2.5 Pro Beta/Theta → 3.0 Flash → 3.0 Pro coming soon).
- **Provider / access:** Agnes AI API, base URL `https://apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1`; three protocol surfaces: OpenAI Chat Completions (`POST /v1/chat/completions`), OpenAI Responses (`POST /v1/responses`), and Anthropic-compatible Messages (`POST /v1/messages`). GA to accounts with Agnes API access; models.dev also catalogs it under the `agnes` provider.
- **Release / knowledge:** released 2026-07 (models.dev release date; `agnes-2.0-flash` predecessor released 2026-05-25 and deprecated — migrations are a model-name change); knowledge cutoff not stated.
- **IDs:** `agnes-2.5-flash` (the only current Flash SKU; `agnes-2.0-flash` deprecated, do not use as fallback).
- **Context window:** 524,288 (512K) total; 65,536 (65.5K) max output — verified from the official limits table. NOTE: the folder's scaffolded meta.json says "128K total", which contradicts the vendor's own docs — 512K is the verified figure.
- **Modalities:** Text + image URL in (publicly accessible `image_url` parts; screenshot analysis, image description, visual Q&A); text out. Tool calling (`tools`/`tool_choice`), streaming, Thinking mode (`chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking` on OpenAI-style; `thinking.budget_tokens` on Anthropic-style, e.g. 2048 for coding tasks); structured agent workflows positioned as a core capability.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** list — $0.05 in / $0.15 out / $0.005 cached per 1M tokens (cached input = 10% of the input price, cache-hit only); **trial — $0 on all three items, and the official pricing page's "Current offers" confirm all three billing items are currently free for `agnes-2.5-flash`** (limited-time; same offer on `agnes-3.0-flash`). Token Plan credits can only be used with Flash models. No free-standing public tier beyond the trial/promo.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed — closed weights, no parameter count, no architecture statement in any official surface.

## Deeper-source sweep (second pass, 2026-11-11)

- **Official pricing page verified in full** (wiki.agnes-ai.com/en/docs/pricing.md): the family table places `agnes-2.5-flash` at $0.05/$0.15/$0.005-cached list with a $0 trial, and the "Current offers" section states input, output and cached input are **currently free** for `agnes-2.5-flash` and `agnes-3.0-flash` — the $0 state is an active limited-time promotion, not the list price. Family price anchors: `agnes-2.5-pro` $0.45/$0.90 (billed, no trial discount), `agnes-2.5-pro-beta` and `-pro-theta` $0.10/$0.30, `agnes-3.0-flash` $0.05/$0.15 (trial free), `agnes-3.0-pro` coming soon at $0.10/$0.30. Cached input is defined as 10% of the input price; Agent Plan usage bills at list price and is excluded from free offers; Token Plan applies to Flash models only.
- **`agnes-3.0-flash` model page** (the successor, released 2026-09): same 512K context / 65,536 output envelope, same text + image-URL input, same three API surfaces and Thinking mode, positioned for agentic coding and tool orchestration ("stronger Agnes Code task execution") — corroborating that the 2.5 Flash spec sheet is the family's stable baseline, and confirming Agnes publishes no benchmark rows for any family member on any docs page.
- Still zero benchmark rows on any surface (official docs and pricing, models.dev, BenchLM 404, web search). The exclusion verdict is unchanged.

